  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A comprehensive approach to recovery of hawksbill turtles in the Eastern Pacific: Protecting one of the last remaining nesting strongholds and spearheading reduction of catastrophic bycatch at critical foraging grounds</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The recipient will work with local communities to build teams to patrol 40 km of hawkbsill nesting beaches from April 15 - October 15 to protect nests through relocation to hatcheries using best management practices, conduct education outreach activities with local communities including an annual Hawksbill Festival &quot;Day of the Hawksbill&quot; activities in local schools, work with local communities to develop eco tourism activities, collect data on lobster fisheries and hawksbill bycatch, and work with local fisherman to develop strategies to reduce hawksbill bycatch . The USFWS will work closely with grantee in setting goals, priorities, and developing budgets, and will also provide assistance as needed and requested in engaging with National Governmental and other institutions to improve collaboration and conservation outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
